// ADR 13.10.26g: a theorem that cites an axiom carries no hole of its own, so
// `check` counts it separately — one hop (`bad2`), two hops (`bad3`) and a
// tactic proof (`bad4`) all rest on `ax`.

axiom ax(): Void
theorem bad2(): Void { ax() }
theorem bad3(): 0 == 1 { absurd(bad2()) }
lemma bad4(): 2 == 3 by { exact absurd(ax()) }
